WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.118 --> 00:00:03.951
- [Narrator] Fancy going shopping?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.264
- Stop!

00:00:06.264 --> 00:00:08.701
No, no, no, no whistling
in the Burlington Arcade.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:09.737
- [Narrator] Uh, who are you?

00:00:09.737 --> 00:00:11.677
- We are the Burlington's Beadles,

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:15.216
probably the oldest and smallest
police force in the world.

00:00:15.216 --> 00:00:17.821
You could say, that we
police your manners.

00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:19.904
- [Narrator] Right, okay.

00:00:22.557 --> 00:00:25.395
Well, Mark Lord, Head Beadle
of the Burlington Arcade,

00:00:25.395 --> 00:00:26.673
tell us your story.

00:00:26.673 --> 00:00:28.049
- The Beadles' story started-

00:00:28.049 --> 00:00:29.526
- [Narrator] Before we get into that,

00:00:29.526 --> 00:00:31.206
what actually is a Beadle?

00:00:31.206 --> 00:00:33.286
- To be honest with you, I don't
think anybody really knows.

00:00:33.286 --> 00:00:36.921
We predate any police
force in the country.

00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:39.398
- [Narrator] Right, back to
the story, go ahead, Mark.

00:00:39.398 --> 00:00:41.706
- The Beadles' story
started at this arcade.

00:00:41.706 --> 00:00:42.539
- [Narrator] Arcade?

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:43.583
Are there games here?

00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:44.416
- No.

00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:45.929
(hearty chuckle)

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:47.866
- [Narrator] So, it's just
like a shopping center right?

00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:48.815
- Yes.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:51.353
- [Narrator] Okay, third
time lucky, go ahead Mark.

00:00:51.353 --> 00:00:55.433
- The Beadles' story started
on the 20th of March 1819.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:57.615
London was very different,
people didn't really

00:00:57.615 --> 00:01:01.076
trust the waters, so they
drank either gin or beer

00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:03.396
and obviously that leads to
a certain type of behavior.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.885
So the Beadles' role, really was to keep

00:01:04.885 --> 00:01:07.215
all that from the arcade and in fact,

00:01:07.215 --> 00:01:10.829
that tradition has carried on
all the way through to today.

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:14.828
Our uniforms are made up of
several different layers.

00:01:14.828 --> 00:01:16.953
We first of all, put on our waistcoats,

00:01:16.953 --> 00:01:19.929
then our frock coats and
our top hats in the summer

00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:22.489
or the autumn, in the winter, you'll still

00:01:22.489 --> 00:01:25.068
put on your waistcoats, you will

00:01:25.068 --> 00:01:28.318
then put on your cape and your top hat.

00:01:30.028 --> 00:01:32.514
The original rules here were, no whistling

00:01:32.514 --> 00:01:35.410
because the pickpockets will
whistle signals to one another.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.772
No drunkenness, playing
musical instrument,

00:01:37.772 --> 00:01:40.711
you're not supposed to
hurry, it's ungentleman-like

00:01:40.711 --> 00:01:42.640
or unlady-like, carry your own parcels,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.898
you mustn't bring a bicycle.
Unaccompanied ladies

00:01:44.898 --> 00:01:47.154
by the way, weren't also allowed in.

00:01:47.154 --> 00:01:50.116
Now, lots of those rules
we couldn't enforce today.

00:01:50.116 --> 00:01:53.399
We've still tried to
enforce the no hurrying,

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:55.298
we still try to enforce the no whistling,

00:01:55.298 --> 00:01:57.958
it's all about behavior, as
long as you're respecting

00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:59.842
those around you and
respecting the arcade,

00:01:59.842 --> 00:02:01.392
you'll be left alone.

00:02:01.392 --> 00:02:03.637
When I put this uniform on, I represent

00:02:03.637 --> 00:02:07.231
nearly 200 years worth of history.

00:02:07.231 --> 00:02:09.630
Makes me immensely
proud, yeah, I wanna stay

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.744
until I retire, if I'm honest with you.

00:02:12.744 --> 00:02:14.067
That's actually true by the way,

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.067
it isn't just the spill.

